  "plain": "In the 1970s, the physicists Hal Puthoff and Russell Targ at SRI, a research institute at Stanford, are said to have run remote-viewing programs, attempts to see distant places with the mind, under the names Stargate and Scanate for the Defense Intelligence Agency and the CIA. A researcher named Maaneli Derakhshani shows Michels an article he says he wrote about these programs, in which Uri Geller and James Randi also come up, and links it to a book called Mind at Large."
